<title>INDIA: 5 India shrs off foreign portfolio holding limits.</title>
<headline>5 India shrs off foreign portfolio holding limits.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India said on Tuesday it has taken five companies off the list of firms in which foreign institutional investor (FII) holdings have reached a 24 percent ceiling.</p>
<p>The firms are: Salora International Ltd, Maral Overseas Ltd, Jai Parabolic Springs Ltd, ModiLuft Ltd and Unitech Ltd.</p>
<p>The central bank also removed three firms -- WS Industries Ltd, MSL Industries Ltd and PVD Plast Mould Ltd -- from a watchlist of firms in which FII holdings have reached 20 percent and needed prior RBI approval for further purchases.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
